{#
  T-4.05 — the hero.

  | Variable                        | Type     | Description                                    |
  |---------------------------------|----------|------------------------------------------------|
  | component                       | object   | Merchant settings from twilight.json           |
  | component.slides[].image        | string   | Image url                                      |
  | component.slides[].alt          | ?string  | Alt text. Empty means decorative — see below   |
  | component.slides[].quote        | ?string  | The line laid over the image                   |
  | component.slides[].url          | ?string  | Where the slide links to                       |
  | component.slides[].strip_start  | ?string  | Info strip, first item (right in RTL)          |
  | component.slides[].strip_center | ?string  | Info strip, middle item                        |
  | component.slides[].strip_end    | ?string  | Info strip, last item (left in RTL)            |
  | component.autoplay              | bool     | Off by default — see WHY AUTOPLAY IS OFF       |
  | position                        | int      | Sorting number, from zero                      |

  BASED ON `enhanced-slider.twig`, NOT A COPY OF IT. Same `salla-slider` carrier
  and the same `type="fullwidth"`, because the platform's slider already handles
  swipe, keyboard and RTL direction and none of that should be rewritten. What
  differs is everything the design changes: the image is an `<img>` rather than a
  CSS background so it can be sized, preloaded and given alt text; the overlay is
  a derived scrim rather than a flat dim; and the three-item strip has no
  upstream analogue at all.

  ALT TEXT IS A MERCHANT FIELD, AND EMPTY IS A VALID ANSWER. Only the merchant
  knows what the image shows. Left blank it renders `alt=""`, which marks the
  image decorative — the correct answer for a banner whose meaning is carried by
  the quote beside it. What is NOT correct is inventing alt text from the store
  name, which is what themes usually do and what makes a screen reader read the
  same words on every slide.

  WHY AUTOPLAY IS OFF BY DEFAULT. WCAG 2.2.2 is a Level A requirement: anything
  that moves for more than five seconds needs a way to stop it. Autoplay is a
  merchant choice, the pause control below appears only when they take it, and
  `home.js` stops it outright under `prefers-reduced-motion`. A slider nobody
  turned on has none of these problems.
#}
{% set hero_slides = component.slides %}
{% set hero_first = hero_slides|first %}

{# LCP. `rel="preload"` is body-ok in HTML, so the hint can be emitted from the
   section rather than requiring the head — which T-3.01 owns and which is not
   done. Only the first slide is preloaded; preloading all ten would compete with
   the one that is actually on screen. #}
{% if hero_first.image %}
    <link rel="preload" as="image" fetchpriority="high" href="{{ hero_first.image }}">
{% endif %}

<section data-testid="store-home-hero" class="s-block hero">
    <salla-slider class="hero__slider"
                  id="hero-{{ position }}"
                  type="fullwidth"
                  static-when-single
                  {{ component.autoplay ? 'auto-play' : '' }}
                  {{ hero_slides|length > 1 ? '' : 'show-controls="false"' }}>
        <div slot="items">
            {% for slide in hero_slides %}
                <div class="swiper-slide hero__slide">
                    <img class="hero__image"
                         src="{{ slide.image }}"
                         alt="{{ slide.alt|default('') }}"
                         width="900"
                         height="1260"
                         {% if loop.first %}fetchpriority="high" loading="eager"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
                         decoding="async">

                    {# The scrim. Not decoration — see hero.scss for the contrast
                       figures that decide its strength. #}
                    <span class="hero__scrim" aria-hidden="true"></span>

                    <div class="hero__content">
                        {% if slide.quote %}
                            <p class="hero__quote">{{ slide.quote }}</p>
                        {% endif %}

                        {% if slide.strip_start or slide.strip_center or slide.strip_end %}
                            <ul class="hero__strip">
                                <li class="hero__strip-item">{{ slide.strip_start }}</li>
                                <li class="hero__strip-item">{{ slide.strip_center }}</li>
                                <li class="hero__strip-item">{{ slide.strip_end }}</li>
                            </ul>
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>

                    {# One stretched link, so the whole slide is clickable and the
                       keyboard still reaches it in a single stop. Its accessible
                       name is the quote, because "الصفحة الرئيسية" repeated per
                       slide tells a screen-reader user nothing. #}
                    {% if slide.url %}
                        <a class="hero__link" href="{{ slide.url }}">
                            <span class="sr-only">{{ slide.quote|default(store.name) }}</span>
                        </a>
                    {% endif %}
                </div>
            {% endfor %}
        </div>
    </salla-slider>

    {#
      Pause / play. Rendered only when the merchant turned autoplay on, because a
      control that stops something already stopped is noise. `home.js` owns its
      behaviour and its pressed state; the label starts as "pause" since autoplay
      is running whenever this button exists.
    #}
    {% if component.autoplay and hero_slides|length > 1 %}
        <button type="button"
                class="hero__autoplay-toggle"
                data-hero-autoplay
                aria-pressed="false"
                aria-label="{{ trans('theme.hero.pause_autoplay') }}">
            {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'pause' } %}
        </button>
    {% endif %}
</section>
